					<Item class="StringValue" referent="414">
						<Properties>
							<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Facet guides

Start with the task you are doing. There is no required chapter sequence.

| Task | Read |
| --- | --- |
| Build or review game UI with an agent | [Use Facet](../../skills/use-facet/SKILL.md) |
| Install and mount a first screen | [Getting started](getting-started.md), [installation](installation.md) |
| Choose behavior | [Control choices](choosing-controls.md) |
| Share state and component ownership | [Components](components.md), [client and server](state.md) |
| Style a game | [Styling](styling.md), [theme packages](themes.md), [skinning](skinning.md) |
| Understand native input | [Input](input.md) |
| Show a course map or radar in the HUD | [Minimaps](minimaps.md) |
| Find a working example | [Examples](examples.md), [made with Facet](made-with-facet.md) |
| Change Facet itself | [Architecture](architecture.md), [maintainers](../MAINTAINERS.md) |
| Validate a change | [Verification scope](verification-scope.md), [devices](device-verification.md), [performance](performance.md) |

Use the [API reference](../reference/api.md) for exact contracts. Its
[task map](../reference/nodes/Map.md) routes to short recipes and control nodes.
The [game UI design guide](../../skills/use-facet/references/GAME_UI_DESIGN_GUIDE.md)
owns design principles; these guides do not duplicate it.
]]></string>
