						<Item class="StringValue" referent="654">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# ProgressView

ProgressView.reference option values and behavior.

The unwrapped value and end label keep their largest measured boxes while their text keeps the same length, as Text does.

On the bar's row, the value and the end label keep the width of their text,
and the track gets the remaining width. When the row is too narrow, the track
becomes narrower first, down to `controls.progress.minTrackWidth`. Only then
does the end label become narrower and end with "…". A short label, such as
"0%" or "3/12", thus always shows in a bar of fixed width.

A bar fills its container's width. Inside a hugging stack or Region form,
give the bar an explicit environment-scaled width with
`Size = UDim2.fromOffset(width, 0)`. A fill child does not size its hugging
parent; it can take the measurement slot's width and keep the form too wide.

| Control | Main contract |
|---|---|
| `ProgressView` | `value`, `min` (0), `max` (1). `presentation`: bar, circular, gauge or spinner. label and endLabel, showValue and format, diameter, thickness, segments, and an optional trail `{ delay, duration }`. The endLabel shows after the value. With a label, a bar shows the value and the endLabel on the label row. Without a label, a bar shows them after the bar, on the bar's row. Segments require the bar presentation. Diameter requires circular, gauge or spinner.  A gauge is a dial: an arc open at the bottom, `sweep` degrees round (60 to 330, default 240), filled to the value, with a needle from the centre to the value and a hub over its root.  `needle = false` leaves only the arc.  A gauge needs a `value`; `sweep` and `needle` refuse every other presentation.  The needle and the hub take the theme's `progress-gauge-needle` and `progress-gauge-hub` roles (content colour). A trail holds on damage, settles over its duration, and snaps on healing or reduced motion. A circular value is centered when the native text bounds fit. Otherwise it shows below the ring. A circular ring with no thickness uses 8 percent of its diameter, and not less than the theme metric. On a bar, `controlSize` sets the track thickness: `xsmall` and `compact` use `space.xs`, and `regular` and `large` use `controls.progress.trackHeight`. A bar refuses `controlSize` together with `thickness`, and a ring or a spinner refuses it together with `diameter`. `endLabel` must be a string. |
]]></string>
