						<Item class="StringValue" referent="691">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Sheet.card

Show temporary modal details.

Inside an app mount, set `local UI = app.UI`.

```luau
UI.Sheet "Sheet" { title = "Details", isPresented = Facet.Compose.cell(true), content = function() return UI.Text { text = "Ready" } end }
```

Key options: `detents`, `placement`, `actions`, `onPresentedChange`.

For a centered task panel, use `placement = "center"`. It shows Close without
a grabber. Use one `hug` detent for short content, or a bounded height for a
collection. Dock at an edge when dragging between task heights helps the player.
A bottom sheet's plate reaches the glass, and its content stays safe.

The content factory takes no arguments and runs when the Sheet is built.
Changing `isPresented` does not rebuild it. Use Compose branches inside the
content; see [State](State.md). Sheet owns scrolling and Back. Use
`onPresentedChange` to guard an unsaved draft.

Related controls: [Controls](Controls.md).

Open:

- [Sheet.reference](Sheet.reference.md)
- [Sheet.dismissal](Sheet.dismissal.md)
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Sheet.card.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">73c8afe78d24b4d30afced1100000690</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="692">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Sheet.detents

Sheet requires a writable `isPresented`. `detent` is a writable cell or a
detent id. With an id or without `detent`, the sheet keeps the selected detent.
It starts at that id, or at the first detent when the id is not in `detents`.
With a cell, the sheet writes the selected detent to the cell. The default
detents are `medium` and `large`. A custom entry is `{ id, fraction }` or
`{ id, height }`, never both. The `hug` entry fits the body and the pinned
regions. It measures the content of the body, not the scroll canvas, so it does
not grow to fill the room. It measures again when the content changes, and it
stays inside the safe room and above a minimum of four target heights.

Supply a `title` and a `content` factory that returns native children. The
sheet calls the factory without arguments. Its subtree fills the body region.
The body uses a native vertical ScrollingFrame named `SheetContent`. Thus
content taller than the selected detent stays reachable, and the sheet chrome
stays fixed.

A fill-height GuiObject receives the body viewport height. This includes a
Frame that composes a fixed composer with its own scrolling message list.

Layout options:
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Sheet.detents.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">73c8afe78d24b4d30afced1100000691</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="693">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Sheet.dismissal

Without `onPresentedChange`, a dismissal writes `false` to `isPresented`.
With `onPresentedChange(nextValue)`, the Sheet proposes `false` and leaves
the cell unchanged. Set the cell to accept. Leave it unchanged to keep the
same mounted content, including its draft and focus, while asking the player.

Close, the dismissible grabber, drag dismissal, outside press, and keyboard
or gamepad Back use this request. `interactiveDismissDisabled` still blocks
interactive dismissal; an explicit Close remains a request. A cancel action
in `actions` owns its callback, so route that callback through the same guard.
Programmatic `isPresented:set(false)` is an accepted model change and does
not invoke the request callback. A content-factory failure still closes the
failed Sheet and reports the error.

For an editor, compare every draft field with accepted state. Use one close
function for the Sheet and other routes that leave the editor:

```luau
local Facet = require(game.ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Facet)
local C = Facet.Compose
local open, dirty, confirmDiscard = C.cell(true), C.cell(false), C.cell(false)
local function requestClose(nextValue: boolean)
    if not nextValue and dirty:peek() then
        confirmDiscard:set(true)
    else
        open:set(nextValue)
    end
end
```

Pass `requestClose` as `onPresentedChange`. Cancel closes only the discard
confirmation. Discard restores the accepted draft, then closes both surfaces.
Save keeps the draft pending until the server accepts it; rejection preserves
the draft and shows the error. See [Tasks.purchase](Tasks.purchase.md) for the
request and response pattern. Do not mark a draft saved when sending a request.

`initialFocus` is a name, or a function that Facet calls once, with no
arguments, when the sheet opens and that returns a name or nil. With a
keyboard or gamepad, the sheet first selects that control, or the first
shown and enabled control inside an instance of that name, in the body or the
actions. Content that mounts after the sheet opens, such as collection rows,
still takes the selection while the player has not moved it. Without it, or when no such control is selectable, it selects the
body's first control, then the action with `role = "default"`, then the
`cancel` action, then the first action that is not `destructive`, and Close or the grabber only
when nothing else can be acted on, since Back already closes the sheet. Name
the item the player most likely wants, such as a recommended product.
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Sheet.dismissal.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">73c8afe78d24b4d30afced1100000692</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="694">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Sheet.drag

Native drag detection resizes docked sheets. Centered sheets do not drag or
show a grabber. Their detents set height without a visible resize affordance.
The grabber detector starts a drag at
once. A second detector on the panel starts a drag only after 6 pixels, or 14
pixels on touch. A release goes to the detent nearest to the released height
plus 0.15 seconds of its velocity. A hold before the release has no velocity.
Below the lowest detent the whole sheet moves down instead of getting shorter,
so the header, the body and the pinned actions move together. A drag below 70
percent of the lowest detent dismisses the sheet, and the exit slide starts
where the drag left it. Past the
limits the drag resists. `interactiveDismissDisabled` holds the sheet near its
lowest detent and blocks Back and the backdrop. An outside detent change
during a drag ends the drag. Only one drag runs at a time.

The grabber sits on the edge that the sheet came from. A bottom
sheet has a horizontal bar at the top. A side sheet from the right has a
vertical bar on its left edge, and a side sheet from the left has one on its
right edge. The grabber sits in its own gutter at that edge, just inside the inner edge
of the theme's panel art (`contentInsets`), centred along the edge. The
content reserves only the gutter, 20 pixels plus an 8 pixel gap, on that side
and keeps equal padding on the other sides. Sheet adds its normal content
spacing inside the theme's panel art insets. The header, body and actions use
this same boundary, including when `contentInset = "none"` removes the body's
extra padding. On a side sheet,
a drag of the grabber toward the sheet's edge moves the whole sheet. A release
past a third of the width, or faster than 600 pixels a second, closes it.
Otherwise it slides back.
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Sheet.drag.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">73c8afe78d24b4d30afced1100000693</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="695">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Sheet.grabber

Docked sheets show a grabber unless `dragIndicator = "hidden"` or an explicit
`closeButton` replaces it. Centered sheets never show one. Hidden grabbers do
not reserve space or participate in selection.

The grabber is also a selectable button. A tap or click closes the sheet
(with `interactiveDismissDisabled` it grows the sheet instead). The engine
gives a press on the grabber to its drag detector and never fires the button's
`Activated`, so a grip drag that ends within 4 pixels of where it started is
the tap. Return or the
gamepad A button grows the sheet to the next taller detent, and its accessible
label reads `Resize: Medium`, or `Resize: Fit` for `hug`. At the tallest
detent, and with one detent, Return or A closes the sheet, and its label reads
`Close sheet`. The grabber's own drag detector
takes a press-drag that starts on the pill, and a release after a drag is not
also a click. The pointer shows a resize cursor over the grabber and a closed
hand while it drags (`SizeNS`, or `SizeEW` on a side sheet, and
`ClosedHand`). Return and the gamepad A button activate it. A bottom
sheet slides up from the bottom and slides down when it closes. The sheet
stays off screen until its room, width, text and height are the same for two
frames, and then it starts to move. Thus the text has its final size and wrap
before the sheet shows, and the height does not change during the slide. With
reduced motion the sheet appears at rest after the same wait. See
[Motion](Motion.md).
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Sheet.grabber.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">73c8afe78d24b4d30afced1100000694</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="696">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Sheet.guide

The Sheet `guide` option pins a ButtonGuide to the bottom edge of the sheet.

- `guide`: [ButtonGuide](ButtonGuide.reference.md) options (`entries`,
  `inputs`, `controlSize`) without native properties. The Sheet puts the
  guide in a `Guide` region at the bottom of the panel, inside the sheet
  padding and below the scrolling `Room` that holds the body and the pinned
  `actions`. The region is outside every scroller, so the guide never scrolls
  away, also when a short sheet scrolls its pinned regions.
- `guideAlignment`: `"end"` (the default, the trailing edge) or `"start"`.

The guide follows the ButtonGuide rules. It shows for its input classes. It
hides when no entry is live and when an Alert opens above the sheet. It is
never a focus stop: a gamepad enters the sheet on its content.

The guide takes its height and an 8 pixel gap from the room above it, so
the body is shorter while the guide shows. While the guide is hidden, the
body takes that room back.

```luau
return UI.Sheet {
    title = "Shop",
    isPresented = Compose.cell(true),
    content = function()
        return UI.Button { label = "Blade" }
    end,
    guide = {
        entries = { { keyCode = { Enum.KeyCode.ButtonL1, Enum.KeyCode.ButtonR1 }, label = "Tabs" } },
    },
    guideAlignment = "start",
}
```
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Sheet.guide.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">73c8afe78d24b4d30afced1100000695</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="697">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Sheet.layout

Placement, width, header, hero, pinned actions, body padding, scroll policy and Close.

- `placement`: `automatic` (the default, the bottom edge), `adaptive`,
  `bottom`, `center` or `side`. On a ten-foot screen `automatic` and
  `adaptive` centre the sheet, and they dock it again when the screen is near. `adaptive` docks the sheet at the side edge
  when the room is 600 pixels wide or more, a mouse is available and touch is
  not. Otherwise it uses the bottom edge. It changes live with the room and
  the input. The `FacetPlacement` attribute of `SheetPanel` holds the result.
  A side sheet docks to `edge` (`left` or `right`, default `right`). `edge`
  also applies to `adaptive`. Its detents stay vertical. It slides in from its edge and leaves
  toward it. Under reduced motion it arrives and leaves at once.
  `center` presents a floating task panel with Close and no grabber or drag
  resizing. Use it for a bounded task such as comparing upgrades. Detents
  still set its height; use one `hug` detent for short intrinsic content.
- `width`: `automatic`, `narrow` or `wide`. These are the Dialog widths:
  `controls.alert.maxWidth`, `controls.popup.panelWidth` and `controls.dialog.wideWidth`. The safe room bounds each one.
- `header`: absent shows `title`. An Instance or a factory replaces the title. `false` removes the title row.
- `hero`: `{ image | content, aspectRatio | height, scaleMode?, background?,
  sticky? }`. A sticky hero stays pinned above the body. Otherwise it scrolls
  with the body. With `header = false`, the close control sits over the hero
  as an `inverse` button, so it reads on any art. Hero `content` is inset 16
  pixels from the sides and 12 from the bottom.
- `actions`: a list of `{ id, label, role?, enabled?, busy?, onActivate }`.
  They stay pinned below the body and never close the sheet. The `default`
  action has the `emphasis` appearance. `actionLayout` is `automatic`, `row`
  or `stacked`. Cancel runs an enabled `role = "cancel"` action first.
- `contentInset`: `standard` or `none`. Standard body padding is 8 pixels
  vertically. Horizontal padding is at least 8 pixels and grows with themed feedback. `none` removes all body padding.
- `scrollPolicy`: `always` (the default) keeps the body scrolling at every height. `atLargestDetent` stops the body scroll below the tallest detent.
- `closeButton`: absent, `true`, `false`, or a string or readable label.
  Absent shows an icon-only Close button in the trailing corner of the
  header when interactive dismissal is enabled and there is no grabber. Its
  accessible name is `Close`, and its target is 44 pixels. `true` always shows
  that icon button and hides the grabber. A label also hides the grabber and
  shows the close icon with that label, so it reads as Close in any language.
  `false` shows none; Back, Escape and the backdrop still close the sheet.

Use one visible dismissal control. A centered sheet has Close. A docked sheet
has a grabber by default. Explicit Close replaces the grabber, and a hidden
grabber reserves no gutter. Leave `closeButton` absent so the control can adapt
when placement changes. Use `false` only when task actions provide a clear exit
in every placement. With disabled interactive dismissal, supply an explicit
Close or task action. A multi-detent grabber expands on Return/A before it
closes at the tallest detent; Back/Escape still provides direct dismissal.
Test the visible exit, Back and return focus on each input.

When the pinned regions and a short body do not fit the panel, every region
moves into one scrolling column named `Room`, so each action stays
reachable. The on-screen keyboard height comes off the room, and the panel
sits above the keyboard.

When a pointer dismisses the keyboard from a TextInput, keep that clearance
until the native InputObject ends or cancels and Compose publishes its next
frame. This keeps an accessory button under the same touch while Roblox
handles activation or cancellation. Keyboard submission releases it directly.
]]></string>
