						<Item class="StringValue" referent="966">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[### ViewThatFits

<!-- aliases: ViewThatFits | viewthatfits -->

`UI.ViewThatFits(spec) -> Frame` shows the first child that fits and hides the
others. Each child is a candidate, in order of preference. The last candidate
shows when none fits. It needs at least one candidate. Options: `width` and
`height`. The props type is `ViewThatFitsProps`.

- With one candidate, its authored `Visible` state stays in control. There is
  no choice to make, so the container does not change that state.
- A candidate fits when its `AbsoluteSize` is not larger than the size of the
  container. Roblox measures every candidate, also a hidden one. Facet only
  sets `Visible`.
- Give the candidates a `hug` or a pixel width. A candidate that fills the
  width always fits.
- A candidate with the `FacetOverflow` attribute set to `true` does not fit
  when the width is tested. A segmented Picker sets it while its strip scrolls,
  so `ViewThatFits { segmented, menu }` shows the menu when the segments do not
  fit on one row.
- The container fills the width and hugs the height by default. An axis that
  hugs is unbounded, so only the width is tested. With a bounded `height`, the
  height is tested too. Directly in a `ScrollView`, the scroll axis is
  unbounded and the first candidate shows.

```luau
UI.ViewThatFits "Actions" {
    UI.HStack { gap = "s", save, cancel, help },
    UI.VStack { gap = "xs", save, cancel, help },
}
```
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">ViewThatFits.reference.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">73c8afe78d24b4d30afced11000007a3</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="967">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# VirtualGrid.card

Virtual tiles.

Inside an app mount, set `local UI = app.UI`. Use a bounded stack:

```luau
local spec: Facet.KeyedCollectionSpec<string, string> = {
    UI.fill(), from = { "Kart" }, key = function(item) return item end,
    minColumnWidth = 180, minColumns = 2, itemSize = 64,
    render = function(current) return UI.Text { text = current } end,
}
local grid: ScrollingFrame = UI.VirtualGrid "Tiles" (spec)
UI.VStack "Browser" { height = "fill", gap = "s",
    UI.Text { text = "Parts" },
    grid,
}
```

`minColumns` can override `minColumnWidth`; allow one column if two make labels
or targets unusable.

Put [fill](fill.md) in the grid spec, not `render`, to use the height left after
headers and gaps.

`measure = true` sizes each row to its tallest native tile, for wrapping or
changing text Cards.

For explicit positions and multi-cell items, use [SpatialGrid](SpatialGrid.card.md).
[Options](VirtualList-and-VirtualGrid.md) or
[content sizing](VirtualList-and-VirtualGrid.sizing.md).
]]></string>
